# The booth is built on Linux from a repository edited on Windows. A shell
# script that arrives with CRLF fails as "bad interpreter: /bin/bash^M", and a
# systemd unit or hostapd.conf with CRLF is rejected just as unhelpfully. Pin
# the line endings for everything that the Pi reads as code or configuration,
# so it no longer depends on each machine's core.autocrlf.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.tmpl          text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf
*.ppd           text eol=lf
config.ini.example text eol=lf
setup/booth.conf.example text eol=lf
